**Seen from the other side.** No core frame leans on ELD. Each ELD unit's host-teacher note (bar item 14) tells the
host teacher the content used and the language taught, so the host can reuse the frames in its own C11 supports.

## For the lead

1. **The C11 gate holds the later stages.** This frame is written under Cory's 2026-11-25 call (DESK-ANSWERS, after-core frames); the scope and sequence, unit plans, days and newcomer strand wait until C11 passes in the probe and guard units of two core subjects, one of them ELA (STANDARD section 6).
2. **Grade 8 owned ids at source.** The parts each grade 8 unit names are drawn from the stored id words (data/standards/wida-2020-words.txt); the framework's own 6-8 expectation lists are not stored locally (S:\CurioClass-sources\WIDA holds the PRIME and rubric files only). A download of the free 2020 framework would let the scope and sequence check every part of the 18 ids at source (no download made).
3. **Row change applied by the lead** (below): g8-ma-argue's Pythagorean lean is later than its unit. If the lead prefers the row as written, the other route is to swap units 19 and 26 (MA Argue last, beside math grade 8 unit 8; SC Explain early, beside science grade 8 unit 1), which leaves s8-natural-selection unused instead.
4. **After-core check days among themselves.** Kept as they are for the lead's one calendar pass (CALENDAR.md rule 3); this frame's mid-year checks are grade 6 days 81 and 82, grade 7 days 85 and 86, grade 8 days 98 and 99, the year-end checks days 158 and 159.
5. **Unused leans.** Five leans are later than every unit that could use them (e7-text-organization, e7-evaluate-argument, m7-two-step-equations in the explain row, e8-paragraph-structure, m8-pythagorean-theorem); each is named with its If later line. The scope and sequence may revisit them; no row change is asked beyond g8-ma-argue.
6. **Newcomer strand time** stays Cory's call, as raised with the pilot (its For the lead, item 6); the same answer covers this band.

