g7-ss-argue | g6-ss-argue | g8-ss-argue | social-studies:ss7-comparing-societies (host unit); social-studies:ss7-research-greek (host unit) | Students compare societies and argue a research claim about ancient Greece, citing sources. Entry points (all compare two societies and argue a research claim about ancient Greece, citing sources): levels 1 and 2 with both societies on the claim chart, a word bank and the cloze "___ had ___, whereas ___ had ___.", the cloze off before the check and the word bank kept; 3 and 4 with "According to ___, ___. Some argue that ___. However, ___.", off before the end-of-unit task; 5 and 6 with the claim chart only, answering another reading and citing a source, the frame gone after the first application day; the grade 6 "used to think" cloze is gone for 3 and 4. Forms: a comparison claim with sources and another view answered; reporting verbs and "Some argue that ___. However, ___"; whereas, compare and society. Home language: a student may plan the comparison in the home language first; sociedad and society, comparar and compare are cognates. Carried, owned in grade 8. In grade 7 comparison claims are added; in grade 8 the "whereas" cloze is gone for levels 3 and 4.

